 Medium Detail Information 
 
 
 
 
 Medium No. 
 
 1020 
 
 
 
 Medium 
 
 Methanofollis ethanolicus medium 
 
 
 
 Composition 
 
 
 
 &nbsp; Ethanol 0.46 ml &nbsp; Yeast extract 0.1 g &nbsp; KH 2 PO 4 0.14 g &nbsp; MgCl 2 &middot;6H 2 O 0.2 g &nbsp; CaCl 2 &middot;2H 2 O 0.15 g &nbsp; NH 4 Cl 0.54 g &nbsp; Sodium acetate 0.82 g &nbsp; Vitamin solution* 2 ml &nbsp; Trace element solution** 2 ml &nbsp; Se/W solution*** 1 ml &nbsp; Resazurin solution**** 1 ml &nbsp; NaHCO 3 2.5 g &nbsp; Na 2 S&middot;9H 2 O 0.3 g &nbsp; Cysteine-HCl 0.3 g &nbsp; Distilled water 1 L &nbsp; &nbsp; For vial cultures, dissolve all ingredients except for ethanol, vitamin solution, Na 2 S&middot;9H 2 O and cysteine-HCl, flush N 2 /CO 2 (80/20) and autoclave. Concentrated Na 2 S&middot;9H 2 O and cysteine-HCl solutions are sterilized separately by autoclaving under a N 2 atmosphere in tightly closed vessels. Add filter-sterilized 0.8 M ethanol and vitamin solutions, and autoclaved Na 2 S&middot;9H 2 O and cysteine-HCl solutions . Inoculum size 10-20%. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; *Vitamin solution &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Biotin 0.5 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Folic acid 0.9 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Pyridoxine-HCl 0.4 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Thiamine-HCl 0.7 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Riboflavin 0.8 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Nicotinic acid 0.2 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Ca-pantothenate 0.5 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Vitamin B 12 2.7 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; p -Aminobenzoic acid 0.3 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Lipoic acid 0.4 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Distilled water 1 L &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; **Trace element solution &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Nitrilotriacetic acid (NTA) 12.8 g &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; FeCl 3 &middot;6H 2 O 1.35 g &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; MnCl 2 &middot;4H 2 O 0.1 g &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; CoCl 2 &middot;6H 2 O 24 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; CaCl 2 &middot;2H 2 O 0.1 g &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ZnCl 2 0.1 g &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; CuCl 2 &middot;2H 2 O 25 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; H 3 BO 3 10 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Na 2 MoO 4 &middot;2H 2 O 24 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; NiCl 2 &middot;6H 2 O 0.12 g &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Distilled water 1 L &nbsp; &nbsp; First dissolve NTA in 200 ml of water and adjust the pH to 6.5 with KOH. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ***Se/W solution &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Na 2 SeO 3 4 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Na 2 WO 4 4 mg &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Distilled water 1 L &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ****Resazurin solution &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Resazurin 1 g &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Distilled water 1 L 
 
 
 
